    "number": 171,
    "title": "docs: add usage examples to cargo-cost-lint README",
    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds practical usage examples to the README, making it easier for developers to get started with `cargo-cost-lint` and interpret its output.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Quick Start section\nTwo-line copy-paste workflow: install the tool, then run it on your project.\n\n### Expanded Usage section\n- Full linter output example showing all three lint warnings with file/line annotations\n- **Storage in a loop** — bad code, linter output, and the fix (accumulate in memory)\n- **Redundant `Env` clone** — bad code and fix (pass by reference)\n- **Host function call in a loop** — bad code and fix (call once, reuse)\n- **Suppressing false positives** — how to use `#[allow(...)]`\n\n### Markdown formatting\nAll code blocks use correctly fenced language tags, headings follow a consistent hierarchy, and rendered output is clean.\n\nCloses #36",
